ede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the middle of the county&rsquo;s grids shows July to August under 90% of normal in 42 of the 75 years since 1951, the most of any pair. In 2025 the middle of the grids ran 34% of normal for September to October and 23% for October to November. So far in 2026, April to May came in at 199% on the middle of the grids. Every grid had its driest year in 2011, and grid 7627 bottomed out at 38% that year.</p>"}
